%% HANDWRITTEN. Checked against ARCHITECTURE.md S12 + D33 as amended by D45 (revised) + D27
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant C as Customer
    participant SYS as ReadyCall
    participant AI as Analysis
    participant A as Agent
    participant OTHER as The agent's OTHER systems
    participant STORE as readycall store

    C->>SYS: hangs up
    SYS->>SYS: agent -> AFTER_CALL_WORK
    Note over SYS,A: the ACW clock starts HERE, at disconnect (D45).<br/>No new call is offered during it.

    par the customer rates, immediately
        SYS->>C: "ให้คะแนน 1 ถึง 5"
        C->>SYS: presses 4
        Note right of C: this happens in seconds, while the<br/>agent has barely started. See Q14.
    and the agent gets a head start
        SYS->>AI: summarise the whole call
        AI-->>A: PRE-FILLED summary + suggested disposition
        Note right of AI: pre-filled, NEVER auto-saved.<br/>The agent owns the record. There is no<br/>timer that writes on their behalf.
    end

    Note over A,OTHER: two independent jobs, in either order

    alt saves the record first
        A->>SYS: edits summary, disposition, SAVE
        SYS->>STORE: call record closed
        A->>OTHER: then does the outside work
    else does the outside work first
        A->>OTHER: another tool, a form, a colleague
        A->>SYS: then SAVE
        SYS->>STORE: call record closed
    end

    A->>SYS: declares the next state
    Note right of A: Ready / Last call -> ACW ends, OFFERABLE<br/>Break / Lunch / Training / Admin -><br/>ACW ends, NOT offerable
    SYS->>SYS: AFTER_CALL_WORK ends

    Note over A,SYS: common case is one click: "Save & Ready".

    Note over STORE: BOTH sides rate (D27). The agent rates the call<br/>too, which is how we learn whether the brief<br/>was actually any good.
